   "version": "Introduced in House",
   "date": "2015-04-28",
   "text": "Keeping Social Security Solvent Act of 2015\n Amends the Internal Revenue Code, with respect to the taxes on employment and self-employment compensation, to repeal the limit on the amount of compensation subject to such taxes (i.e., the contribution and benefit base, currently $118,500 in 2015)."
  }
